trix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 9 \\\\ 5 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}19 & 9 \\\\ 9 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "22274fb1-dba1-5685-b7c6-d45b7e3adb09"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551388 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162602 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6bd7ec03-edfe-5cbf-9100-12b8bdb0c709" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355618} {:answer/id #uuid "8d438ce4-5f0a-5c5e-9315-d5ef9dd4deac" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355912} {:answer/id #uuid "8f15bd83-407e-5af6-bdf7-c2bbd68497da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355927} {:answer/id #uuid "b0b80b83-2a99-5e5e-9139-10034e099578" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}+5{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-2{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356221} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1ab829-69f5-5348-881b-7cec2de50e44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356336}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186356336} :answer-field/id #uuid "c6f0ff43-58b3-5468-9256-34c2b09001cc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357275}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "9c51ecf1-6711-57f2-8c41-d6bd2fed54f1" :question/math-academy-id "q-93735" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1}+2{x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the second equation for ${x}_{2}$ and substituting it into the first equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1}+2{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+3{x}_{1}{x}_{2}+{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})^{2}+3({y}_{1}+2{y}_{2})(-{y}_{2})+(-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+4{y}_{2}^{2}-3{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-6{y}_{2}^{2}+{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "37c7cf3a-8392-5826-b9ec-d90c9519cc93" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551451}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551409 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378025 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22de68e6-1c43-5759-8e78-082973f85315" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}5 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378027} {:answer/id #uuid "b51565a2-2a7f-5078-a562-c70e16356c9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378028} {:answer/id #uuid "a44bc406-8b4f-5f40-900f-52285c2297ea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378029} {:answer/id #uuid "3d625d43-2367-5b2f-8004-88a324378eab" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 2 \\\\ 2 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378030} {:answer/id #uuid "28b3f821-1757-5da5-8fd7-b4da0d85d08a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378031}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186378028} :answer-field/id #uuid "11ac9437-9c15-579b-9a0f-02533988b38a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186378026}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "556f278c-cc57-5b03-9c66-f86e191b363d" :question/math-academy-id "q-94186" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix},\\,P=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices $A$ and $P$ above. Find the matrix of the quadratic form ${x}^{T}\\,Ax$ in the basis that consists of the columns of $P.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that if $x=[{x}_{1},{x}_{2}]^{T}$ is a vector given by its coordinates in the standard basis and $y=[{y}_{1},{y}_{2}]^{T}$ is the same vector but given in the coordinates relative to the basis that consists of the columns of $P,$ then \n\n$$\nx=Py.\n$$\n\nAs a result, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{T}\\,Ax & =(Py)^{T}\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & =({y}^{T}{P}^{T})\\,A\\,(Py) \\\\  & ={y}^{T}({P}^{T}\\,AP)\\,y,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich means that the matrix of our form in the new basis is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}^{T}\\,AP & ={\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}}^{T}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 5 \\\\ 4 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & 5 \\\\ 5 & 11\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "64524a47-5e0e-5053-bd6f-0e2b585cdcb5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551374}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551451 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186357678 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15af3a2b-005d-589c-8b51-669da6c394e1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186354860} {:answer/id #uuid "7f254103-da65-5ea6-b832-fc5c91c6296f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-5{y}_{1}^{2}-7{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355782} {:answer/id #uuid "83decb3b-6b70-5f63-8936-7619a5f23daf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-3{y}_{1}^{2}-9{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355826} {:answer/id #uuid "98e4be99-59c3-5ae9-82db-7f1009beb920" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{y}_{1}^{2}+4{y}_{1}{y}_{+}{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356019} {:answer/id #uuid "cbb47751-829f-5aab-b494-00d0a3d96200" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "5{y}_{1}^{2}-6{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356441}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355782} :answer-field/id #uuid "70d14260-2556-52c8-a989-5191e23d9daa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357116}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "8e3709ff-318c-5598-82d8-cdf2103d7ab9" :question/math-academy-id "q-94166" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}-{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy solving the first equation for ${x}_{1}$ and substituting it into the second equation, we obtain the following expressions for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & ={y}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} & =-{y}_{1}-{y}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+5{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}+5{y}_{1}(-{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})-(-{y}_{1}-{y}_{2})^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{1}^{2}-5{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =-5{y}_{1}^{2}-7{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "d147e2e2-aa64-5057-9352-9369e34a44e5" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551463}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551463 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162621 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33dce4c6-a921-5609-a40b-0f4435c0ccee" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355121} {:answer/id #uuid "46f2051a-aab6-587b-87a9-8dfa3788d3ba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "2{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355293} {:answer/id #uuid "79515c5d-06a7-5dad-bb16-30c2d00d6bc7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186355724} {:answer/id #uuid "dfe4a971-fd4a-50c9-8577-26d6033f2374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{y}_{1}^{2}-2{y}_{1}{y}_{2}-{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356623} {:answer/id #uuid "e286ef9f-50be-51f3-a6b4-b463e95fcc16" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{y}_{1}^{2}+{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186356648}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186355121} :answer-field/id #uuid "ec481405-702c-50ef-b886-aad868046c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186357332}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487} :question/id #uuid "28be3e2f-b0ff-5855-af78-c4f12425ac89" :question/math-academy-id "q-94180" :question/problem "Given that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix},\n$$\n\n express the quadratic form $Q(x)={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2}$ in terms of the components of $y.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that \n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{y}_{1} \\\\ {y}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\ngives the following expressions for ${y}_{1}$ and ${y}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}_{1} & ={x}_{2} \\\\ {y}_{2} & =-{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSolving these for ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =-{y}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}_{1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we substitute these into our quadratic form expression:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Q(x) & ={x}_{1}^{2}+{x}_{1}{x}_{2}-2{x}_{2}^{2} \\\\  & =(-{y}_{2})^{2}+(-{y}_{2}){y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & ={y}_{2}^{2}-{y}_{2}{y}_{1}-2{y}_{1}^{2} \\\\  & =-2{y}_{1}^{2}-{y}_{1}{y}_{2}+{y}_{2}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :step/id #uuid "e7ce4ba0-2394-5109-8b2f-c042da1d0452" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186551409}}] :activity/title "Change of Variables in Quadratic Forms" :activity/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186550363}]}
